// What Ruby says to the shared scope rules: a local variable exists from its first assignment in
// the method, class body or program (or in the block that makes it, when no scope around the block
// has it), a method, class or module sees none of the names around it, a block sees all of them.
// Format: core_semantics::scopes::rows.
names Identifier Label
labels Label
methods Def
blocks Block Lambda
interpolated HeredocBody
unused-prefix _

Program var-scope
Def var-scope closed
Class var-scope closed
Module var-scope closed
SingletonClass var-scope closed
// A parameter: the first name token of the node.
RequiredParameter declares=value|parameter token=first/declare
OptionalParameter declares=value|parameter token=first/declare
RestParameter declares=value|parameter token=first/declare
RequiredKeywordParameter declares=value|parameter token=first/declare
OptionalKeywordParameter declares=value|parameter token=first/declare
KeywordRestParameter declares=value|parameter token=first/declare
BlockParameter declares=value|parameter token=first/declare
LocalVariableRead reference
// A node whose first name token is a local variable that is written (`x = 1`, `x += 1`; a target
// of `a, b = ...`, `for x in`, `rescue => x`: a plain write).
LocalVariableWrite token=first/assign."=" implicit=value|let@unseen
LocalVariableOperatorWrite token=first/assign."=" implicit=value|let@unseen
LocalVariableOrWrite token=first/assign."=" implicit=value|let@unseen
LocalVariableAndWrite token=first/assign."=" implicit=value|let@unseen
LocalVariableTarget token=first/write implicit=value|let@unseen
